markets price Shapiro's win probability at 96-97%"], "rationale": "Polling across the year shows a stable, wide Shapiro lead, his money advantage is overwhelming, and every rater and market treats the race as safely Democratic; the state's slight Republican lean is the only drag on an otherwise dominant incumbent position.", "watch": "Only an unexpected late scandal or a sharp shift in the national midterm environment could compress a lead this wide.", "confidence": "high", "notes": ["Incumbent Josh Shapiro (D) is running."]}, "overview": "Josh Shapiro seeks a second term as Pennsylvania governor against State Treasurer Stacy Garrity, with Libertarian Ken Krawchuk also on the ballot. Every major race rating outfit places the contest in the Democratic column, most calling it solid or safe. Polling since spring has consistently shown Shapiro well ahead, with the most recent high-quality surveys putting his lead near twenty points, and even Republican-sponsored polls show him comfortably in front.\n\nShapiro holds a large advantage in fundraising and advertising, and headlines through early October emphasize the lopsided nature of the contest in money, name recognition, and polling. Garrity, a statewide officeholder, has struggled to close the gap despite contrasts on education funding, taxes, and affordability. Prediction markets price Shapiro's reelection chances near ninety-seven percent. Pennsylvania's slight Republican lean matters little against an incumbent with this polling and financial edge.", "history": [{"date": "2026-09-22", "p_dem": 0.9929, "margin": 15.66}, {"date": "2026-09-23", "p_dem": 0.9928, "margin": 16.0}, {"date": "2026-09-24", "p_dem": 0.9978, "margin": 19.5}, {"date": "2026-09-25", "p_dem": 0.9956, "margin": 18.0}, {"date": "2026-09-26", "p_dem": 0.9951, "margin": 17.5}, {"date": "2026-09-27", "p_dem": 0.995, "margin": 17.5}, {"date": "2026-09-28", "p_dem": 0.995, "margin": 17.5}, {"date": "2026-09-29", "p_dem": 0.9972, "margin": 20.0}, {"date"